## The Allergen Avalanche

In the year so far, allergens have been the most reported issue, making up a staggering 40% (311 cases) of all food recalls. This trend continues with some significant entries noted just recently. For example, Adams Extract & Spice LLC alone has multiple products recalled due to undeclared sesame allergen, including their "Smoked Sausage Spice" and "Coopers Bbq 60 Gal Bean Mix".

## Salmonella: A Persistent Threat

Salmonella contamination creeps back into the spotlight with Trafa Pharmaceutical Inc.'s "ORGANIC MORINGA LEAF POWDER", a surprising non-food item, marking a Class I recall. This shows that even non-edible products in the food chain can pose risks.

## Foreign Object Findings

Finally, a peculiar recall by Wondermade LLC reveals the presence of small metal pieces in their "Alabama Banana Pudding Marshmallow". This is a reminder that foreign object contamination isn't limited to large-scale manufacturing mishaps; niche and artisanal brands hold equal accountability.
